WebAuthnValidator::isValidSignature
├── given the account has no installed pubkey
│   └── when any signature is checked
│       └── it should return false (sentinel: both coords zero)
├── given the account has installed a pubkey
│   ├── when the signature is a well-formed but invalid WebAuthnAuth
│   │   └── it should return false (verification fails, no revert)
│   └── when the signature blob is not decodable as a WebAuthnAuth
│       └── it should revert (abi.decode of garbage)
└── given the account has installed a pubkey [KNOWN GAP]
    └── when a fully valid P256 WebAuthnAuth over the challenge is supplied
        └── it should return true  (NOT COVERED — needs a real P256 fixture; see notes)
